        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0844" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-23T14:00:00-03:00">June 23, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>38. This Embassy’s despatch No. 3600 dated May 20.<anchor n="64" xml:id="d567-f1"
                    /> Yesterday, at the weekly diplomatic audience, the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs again pointed out that the dangerous tension which existed between
                    Bolivia and Paraguay was increasing. He is of the opinion that measures should
                    be taken to induce Bolivia and Paraguay to accept the double arbitration set
                    forth in that despatch. While the Minister did not say so, Brazil is evidently
                    prepared to assume some interested part in the [proposed?] reconciliation which
                    it declined to do at the time of the appointment of the neutral committee.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
